-- title:
--   Theorem 3.3(4), p. 7 — ℙ_x(T_[b < ζ) (3.11) and the density of G^[b (3.12) (part 4 of 4; companions theorem_3_3_1, _2, _3)
-- statement:
--   Let $E=[\mathfrak l,\mathfrak h]\cap\mathbb Z$ and let $(X,\mathbb P)$ be the Markov chain with state space $E$ generated by a Q-matrix $Q$ (not necessarily conservative) that is skip-free downward, i.e. satisfies (2.1): $Q(x,x-1)>0$ for $x>\mathfrak l$ and $Q(x,y)=0$ for $y\le x-2$. Assume all states are transient and fix a reference point $\mathfrak o\in E$. Write $G$ for the resolvent, $\zeta$ for the lifetime and $T_A$ for the first hitting time of $A$. Let $H$, $\widehat H$, $\mathbf H^{[b}$ and $\mathfrak C$ be as in Theorem 3.1. Let $\pi$ be the positive excessive reference measure, $b\in E$, $E^{[b}=E\cap(-\infty,b)$, and $G^{[b}$ the resolvent of the chain killed on entering $[b,\infty)$, with density $\mathfrak g^{[b}=G^{[b}/\pi$.
--
--   If $\mathfrak l=-\infty$, the limit $\mathbf H^{[b}(-\infty):=\lim_{x\to-\infty}\mathbf H^{[b}(x)$ exists in $(0,\infty]$. For $x\in E$,
--   $$\mathbb P_x(T_{[b}<\zeta)=\begin{cases}1-\sum_{z\in E^{[b}}Q(z,\partial)G^{[b}(x,z)-\dfrac{\mathbf H^{[b}(x)}{\mathbf H^{[b}(-\infty)}, & \mathfrak l=-\infty,\\[6pt] 1-\sum_{z\in E^{[b}}Q(z,\partial)G^{[b}(x,z), & \mathfrak l>-\infty,\end{cases}\tag{3.11}$$
--   and for $x,y\in E^{[b}$
--   $$\mathfrak g^{[b}(x,y)=\mathfrak C\,\widehat H(y)\big(\mathbf H^{[b}(x)-\mathbf H^{[y}(x)\big).\tag{3.12}$$
--
--   This is the upward first-passage identity; when $\mathfrak l=-\infty$ the last term accounts for escape to $-\infty$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: E = [𝔩, 𝔥] ∩ ℤ with 𝔩 < 𝔥 in ℤ ∪ {±∞} → E : Set ℤ with E.OrdConnected and two points x < y in E (𝔩 = −∞ iff ¬ BddBelow E, 𝔥 = ∞ iff ¬ BddAbove E); reason: an order-connected subset of ℤ with at least two points is exactly such an integer interval
--   - encoding: all states in E are transient → AllTransient E Q: G(x, x) < ∞ for every x ∈ E; reason: Norris, Markov Chains, Theorem 3.4.2, which the paper itself invokes on p. 3; an absorbing state has G(x, x) = ∞
--   - encoding: the Markov chain (X, ℙ) generated by Q (jump chain/holding time definition, p. 2) → transition, resolvent, hitProb, hitBeforeProb, exitDist, killedResolvent computed from jump-chain path sums with Exp(1) holding clocks; reason: this is the paper's construction (i)–(iv); the cemetery ∂ is represented by leaving E
--   - encoding: the fixed positive excessive reference measure π of p. 3 (standing for Section 3) → explicit hypotheses π : ℤ → ℝ, ∀ x ∈ E, 0 < π x, IsExcessiveMeasure E Q π; reason: the section's standing assumption written into the binders
--   - encoding: real-valued probabilities ℙ_x(…) → ℝ≥0∞-valued path sums compared through .toReal; reason: a probability is at most 1, so .toReal loses nothing
--   - encoding: H^{[b}(−∞) ∈ (0, ∞] and the ratio H^{[b}(x)/H^{[b}(−∞) → ∃ L : ℝ≥0∞, L ≠ 0, ofReal H^{[b}(x) → L as x → −∞; the ratio is (ofReal H^{[b}(x) / L).toReal; reason: extended-real limit; the ratio is 0 when L = ∞, as the paper intends
--   - encoding: ∑_{z ∈ E^{[b}} Q(z, ∂) G^{[b}(x, z) (an infinite sum when 𝔩 = −∞) → ℝ≥0∞ tsum over z ∈ ℤ of ofReal(Q(z, ∂)) · G^{[b}(x, z), with a finiteness clause, then .toReal; reason: G^{[b}(x, ·) vanishes outside E^{[b}, Q(z, ∂) ≥ 0; the sum is at most 1 so the clause is part of the paper's real formula
--   - reading: the notation of Theorem 3.1: H(x), H^{[y}(x) = lim_{y↓𝔩} …, Ĥ(y) = lim_{x↑𝔥} … (no printed case split for H^{[b} and Ĥ) → fundH, fundHb, fundHhat: value at 𝔩 (resp. 𝔥) when E is bounded below (resp. above), limUnder along atBot (resp. atTop) otherwise; existence of these limits is asserted in theorem_3_1_1 and theorem_3_1_3; reason: the paper defines the notation lim_{y↓𝔩} by this case split for H in Theorem 3.1(1); Theorem 3.3 is stated 'using its notation'
-- source:
--   Loeffen, Patie, Wang, Fluctuation Theory of Continuous-Time, Skip-Free Downward Markov Chains with Applications to Branching Processes with Immigration, arXiv:2208.14425v1, p. 7, Theorem 3.3(4), (3.11)–(3.12)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SkipFreeFluct_MBI_Chain
open scoped ENNReal Topology
open Filter MeasureTheory

namespace SkipFreeFluct.MBI

/-- Theorem 3.3(4), p. 7, (3.11)–(3.12). Under the assumptions of Theorem 3.1 (with the positive
excessive reference measure `π`), for `b ∈ E`:
if `𝔩 = -∞`, the limit `H^{[b}(-∞) := lim_{x → -∞} H^{[b}(x)` exists in `(0, ∞]` and
`ℙ_x(T_{[b} < ζ) = 1 - ∑_{z ∈ E^{[b}} Q(z, ∂) G^{[b}(x, z) - H^{[b}(x)/H^{[b}(-∞)`;
if `𝔩 > -∞`, `ℙ_x(T_{[b} < ζ) = 1 - ∑_{z ∈ E^{[b}} Q(z, ∂) G^{[b}(x, z)` (the killing sum is
finite in both cases); and (3.12) `𝔤^{[b}(x, y) = ℭ Ĥ(y) (H^{[b}(x) - H^{[y}(x))` for
`x, y ∈ E^{[b} = E ∩ (-∞, b)`. -/
theorem theorem_3_3_4 (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (hE : IsStateSpace E) (hQ : IsQMatrix E Q)
    (hS : SkipFreeDown E Q) (hT : AllTransient E Q) (o : ℤ) (ho : o ∈ E)
    (π : ℤ → ℝ) (hπpos : ∀ x ∈ E, 0 < π x) (hπ : IsExcessiveMeasure E Q π)
    (b : ℤ) (hb : b ∈ E) :
    (∀ x ∈ E, ∑' z : ℤ,
        ENNReal.ofReal (killRate E Q z) * killedResolvent E Q (Set.Ici b) x z ≠ ⊤) ∧
    (¬ BddBelow E →
      ∃ L : ℝ≥0∞, L ≠ 0 ∧
        Tendsto (fun x : ℤ => ENNReal.ofReal (fundHb E Q o b x)) atBot (𝓝 L) ∧
        ∀ x ∈ E,
          (hitProb E Q (Set.Ici b) x).toReal =
            1 - (∑' z : ℤ,
                ENNReal.ofReal (killRate E Q z) * killedResolvent E Q (Set.Ici b) x z).toReal
              - (ENNReal.ofReal (fundHb E Q o b x) / L).toReal) ∧
    (BddBelow E → ∀ x ∈ E,
      (hitProb E Q (Set.Ici b) x).toReal =
        1 - (∑' z : ℤ,
            ENNReal.ofReal (killRate E Q z) * killedResolvent E Q (Set.Ici b) x z).toReal) ∧
    ∀ x ∈ E, ∀ y ∈ E, x < b → y < b →
      killedRdens E Q π (Set.Ici b) x y =
        rdens E Q π o o * fundHhat E Q π o y * (fundHb E Q o b x - fundHb E Q o y x) := by sorry

end SkipFreeFluct.MBI
